{"type":"text","timestamp":1788164641811,"sessionID":"ses_fa9158e51ffe06kpEfMXBMQYJc","part":{"id":"prt_056eb0dfe0017u8FbPjGqzqr6d","messageID":"msg_056eafb6b001jkQJrWeIJK9CMY","sessionID":"ses_fa9158e51ffe06kpEfMXBMQYJc","type":"text","text":"Initial failures are environmental rather than code-level: `python` is unavailable and `python3` has no `pytest` installed. The defect is localized to `orders.adapter`: it reads `product.price_cents` and top-level `product.currency`, while the new catalog stores both values under `product.price`. I’ll make the adapter normalize both shapes, leaving order/report aggregation intact and retaining explicit mixed-currency rejection.","time":{"start":1788164640254,"end":1788164641803},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"msg_0a235292a5c58a72016a953a202c9487d2bbaf3e59b5ed6cd4","phase":"commentary"}}}}
