{"type":"text","timestamp":1788164674482,"sessionID":"ses_fa9158e51ffe06kpEfMXBMQYJc","part":{"id":"prt_056eb92920014iuSghujowdY9T","messageID":"msg_056eb80fd001VaVf7puo9BerH9","sessionID":"ses_fa9158e51ffe06kpEfMXBMQYJc","type":"text","text":"The production fix now passes manual equivalents of all visible integration cases: `Money` products, legacy dictionaries, per-currency reporting, and mixed-currency rejection with currency names in the error. I’m recording the environment limitation and verification details in the requested report path mapped to `/workspace/out`.","time":{"start":1788164674194,"end":1788164674481},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"msg_06ce082cc8e4df18016a953a416b4887d28e010da5cbcbdf5b","phase":"commentary"}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788164680887,"sessionID":"ses_fa9158e51ffe06kpEfMXBMQYJc","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"apply_patch","callID":"call_Zagzv8ilLCImRusXVxMa4eNu","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"patchText":"*** Begin Patch\n*** Add File: /workspace/out/interface_fix_report.md\n+# Interface Fix Report\n+\n+## Root Cause\n+\n+`catalog` now exposes a product's price as `product.price`, a `Money` object whose fields are `amount_cents` and `currency`. `orders.adapter` still read the removed `product.price_cents` and top-level `product.currency` attributes, so current catalog products could not be priced. The adapter also needed to continue accepting legacy dictionaries with `price_cents`.\n+\n+## Changed Files\n+\n+- `packages/orders/orders/adapter.py`: read `Money.amount_cents` and `Money.currency` for current products, while retaining the legacy dictionary path.\n+- `packages/orders/orders/service.py`: preserve mixed-currency rejection and include both currencies in the error for clarity.\n+\n+The `catalog` `Money` model and the reports aggregation contract were left unchanged.\n+\n+## Verification\n+\n+Requested command:\n+\n+```text\n+python -m pytest tests\n+```\n+\n+It could not run in this environment because `python` is unavailable. The equivalent `python3 -m pytest tests` also could not run because `pytest` is not installed. A direct `python3` integration check with `PYTHONPATH=packages/catalog:packages/orders:packages/reports` passed for current `Money` products, legacy dictionaries, per-currency reports, and mixed-currency rejection.\n*** End Patch"},"output":"Success. Updated the following files:\nA workspace/out/interface_fix_report.md","metadata":{"diff":"Index: /workspace/out/interface_fix_report.md\n===================================================================\n--- /workspace/out/interface_fix_report.md\n+++ /workspace/out/interface_fix_report.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,22 @@\n+# Interface Fix Report\n+\n+## Root Cause\n+\n+`catalog` now exposes a product's price as `product.price`, a `Money` object whose fields are `amount_cents` and `currency`. `orders.adapter` still read the removed `product.price_cents` and top-level `product.currency` attributes, so current catalog products could not be priced. The adapter also needed to continue accepting legacy dictionaries with `price_cents`.\n+\n+## Changed Files\n+\n+- `packages/orders/orders/adapter.py`: read `Money.amount_cents` and `Money.currency` for current products, while retaining the legacy dictionary path.\n+- `packages/orders/orders/service.py`: preserve mixed-currency rejection and include both currencies in the error for clarity.\n+\n+The `catalog` `Money` model and the reports aggregation contract were left unchanged.\n+\n+## Verification\n+\n+Requested command:\n+\n+```text\n+python -m pytest tests\n+```\n+\n+It could not run in this environment because `python` is unavailable. The equivalent `python3 -m pytest tests` also could not run because `pytest` is not installed. A direct `python3` integration check with `PYTHONPATH=packages/catalog:packages/orders:packages/reports` passed for current `Money` products, legacy dictionaries, per-currency reports, and mixed-currency rejection.\n\n","files":[{"filePath":"/workspace/out/interface_fix_report.md","relativePath":"workspace/out/interface_fix_report.md","type":"add","patch":"Index: /workspace/out/interface_fix_report.md\n===================================================================\n--- /workspace/out/interface_fix_report.md\n+++ /workspace/out/interface_fix_report.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,22 @@\n+# Interface Fix Report\n+\n+## Root Cause\n+\n+`catalog` now exposes a product's price as `product.price`, a `Money` object whose fields are `amount_cents` and `currency`. `orders.adapter` still read the removed `product.price_cents` and top-level `product.currency` attributes, so current catalog products could not be priced. The adapter also needed to continue accepting legacy dictionaries with `price_cents`.\n+\n+## Changed Files\n+\n+- `packages/orders/orders/adapter.py`: read `Money.amount_cents` and `Money.currency` for current products, while retaining the legacy dictionary path.\n+- `packages/orders/orders/service.py`: preserve mixed-currency rejection and include both currencies in the error for clarity.\n+\n+The `catalog` `Money` model and the reports aggregation contract were left unchanged.\n+\n+## Verification\n+\n+Requested command:\n+\n+```text\n+python -m pytest tests\n+```\n+\n+It could not run in this environment because `python` is unavailable. The equivalent `python3 -m pytest tests` also could not run because `pytest` is not installed. A direct `python3` integration check with `PYTHONPATH=packages/catalog:packages/orders:packages/reports` passed for current `Money` products, legacy dictionaries, per-currency reports, and mixed-currency rejection.\n","additions":22,"deletions":0}],"diagnostics":{},"truncated":false},"title":"Success. Updated the following files:\nA workspace/out/interface_fix_report.md","time":{"start":1788164680882,"end":1788164680885}},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"fc_06ce082cc8e4df18016a953a4262b087d28f5a3f82b4ea9dea"}},"id":"prt_056eb93bf001N5TFdgYPf6pJV3","sessionID":"ses_fa9158e51ffe06kpEfMXBMQYJc","messageID":"msg_056eb80fd001VaVf7puo9BerH9"}}
